# ============================================================================
# What is NOT committed, and why.
#
# The rule applied throughout: ignore things that are GENERATED or LOCAL, keep
# things that are EVIDENCE or SOURCE. Anything ambiguous is kept, because a
# missing file costs more than a slightly larger repository.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED (do not add rules that would catch these):
#   docs/       the architecture record, ADRs and reports -- the point of the POC
#   scripts/    including scripts/report.py, which generates the HTML reports
#   reports/    the generated per-execution HTML is kept as a deliverable
#   configs/    every bind-mounted service config
#   images/     every Docker build context
#   tests/      the test suite
#   benchmark/  the harness AND benchmark/results/, which docs/benchmark-report.md
#               cites by filename as the evidence behind its published numbers.
#               Ignoring results would orphan every figure in that report.
# ============================================================================

# --- generated secrets and local state --------------------------------------
# pki/ holds a CA private key and a server private key, regenerated by
# ./scripts/gen-certs.sh. Never commit a private key.
pki/

# Local configuration; .env.example is the committed template.
.env

# --- AI agent artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
# prompt.md is the original brief handed to the coding agent -- working notes,
# not part of the deliverable. Likewise any agent/tool state directory.
prompt.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.github/copilot*

# --- editor / OS junk -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- transient build/test output --------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
